    "hobbies": "1) concerts!: i'm obsessed with going to concerts. i've been trying to keep count and right now i'm at 37 total. music is really important to me and i love seeing all of my favorite artists live! i always bring my digicam to take pics and videos, and it's also just have a lot of fun getting ready/dressing up, collecting merch, and spending time with my friends and girlfriend 2) thrifting: i looove thrifting the majority of my clothes/accessories. some of my favorite places to go are crossroads, black&brown, moon zooom, and of course goodwill. i definitely want to go to the bins more often as well. i love the thrill of finding things for super cheap and i prefer vintage quality and designs/styles. i love shopping in general so thrifting is also a really good way to not spend as much 3) driving/hanging out with friends around the bay area: i'm super grateful to be able to live in the bay area and i loveee to drive around and explore new places. over the summer, i made a list of all cities surrounding san jose within a 50 mile radius and made it my goal to visit all of them, and i completed almost all of it! and of course i also love going to sf and santa cruz 4) nails: i've been doing my own gel-x nails for the past four years. i used to be really into drawing when i was younger, but i don't have a lot of time to draw in college. doing nails has been a really good way for me to be creative while also doing a service that feels productive. it also saves a lot of money! 5) volunteering: last year, i wasn't very involved in anything at sjsu besides going to class, so this semester i've been picking up volunteering shifts at the spartan food pantry and the community garden. it feels really good to know that you're helping out your peers and also meet new people in the process",
