    "hobbies": "Traveling: I like to go to different countries (sometimes solo) to explore the culture and try different types of food. Countries I have been to so far include Viet (of course), Japan, Korea, and Taiwan. Traveling solo increases by confidence by pushing me out of my comfort zone and making me feel more independent. I would like to travel more of the world someday, but time and money is the restraint. Researching spots to go for future trips is very fun as well. Exploring nature: I like to go on hikes and just get lost in nature and just relax at certain spots while doing nothing in particular. I can spend a long time just staring at waterfalls or the ocean side because of how calming it feels. I just wish San Jose had more spots to explore so I can go hiking more often. Watching anime: it's kind of hard to really get into a show I really like, but when I do, I love a good binge. I think at this point, I've probably watched over 150 shows (I never skip the openings or endings). Some of my favorites include 86, Parasyte, Tokyo Ghoul, Gintama, Hibike Euphonium, Re:zero, and That Time I got Reincarnated as a Slime. Some shows really helped improve my mood when I was feeling down. I think Shounen shows are really cool, but I also really like slice of life and romance. Although I really like anime, I don't think I would really buy anime merch or go to conventions or anything. However, I find it really fun to discuss shows with others, especially when they are currently airing or recent. Going to church: as a Catholic, I enjoy learning more about my faith and like the sense of community. Listening to Bible readings helps inspire and lead me to become a better person and learn how to live a better life. My faith has played a really important role in my life and helped me when times were tough. Sometimes, my church holds events or fairs where there is lion dancing, and it is pretty fun. Sometimes I go to mass in English, but mostly I go in Vietese, so that is a good opportunity to practice my Viet listening skills!",
    "music": "My favorite genre is R&B or pop. A couple of songs include: -Dancing with my phone by HYBS -It's not living (if it's not with you) by the 1975 -Home by Luke Chiang -odoriko by Vaundy",
